      "slot": "G",
      "plays_role": "External negentropy influx — the outside source that keeps the coherence of the resurrection testimony from dissipating into myth. For Habermas, this is the pre-Pauline creedal tradition that enters the historical record from outside Paul's own authorship and before his conversion.",
      "quote": "They said that creed or its component parts was already in existence before Paul took his walk to Damascus. [S388]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "M",
      "plays_role": "Alignment — the coupling between the researcher and the evidence. Habermas aligns with the data by reading critics and believers equally, refusing to prejudge who is a Christian.",
      "quote": "I have no right to label somebody a Christian or a non-Christian. [S015]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "E",
      "plays_role": "Signal fidelity — whether the historical truth survives transmission through the noise of scholarly distortion and myth. The early creeds are the signal that must not be corrupted.",
      "quote": "What keeps the creeds from being expanded until they become myth? And they're not really the words of the eyewitnesses. [S401-S402]",
      "fit": "direct"
    },
    {
      "slot": "S_eff",
      "plays_role": "Effective entropy — the noise that lowers coherence: the gap between the resurrection event and the written sources, which critics claim allows myth to develop.",
      "quote": "33 to 48 is only 15 years. That's really But if you go with me with I'd say 30 to 50, that's 20 years. That's earlier than Mark, earlier in all the gospels. [S350-S352]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "T",
      "plays_role": "Temporal integration — the accumulation of historical consequence over time. The shorter the gap between event and creed, the stronger the case; time turns possibility into accumulated evidence.",
      "quote": "33 to 48 is only 15 years. That's really But if you go with me with I'd say 30 to 50, that's 20 years. That's earlier than Mark, earlier in all the gospels. [S350-S352]",
      "fit": "direct"
    },
    {
      "slot": "K",
      "plays_role": "Compression — ordered meaning compresses and noise does not. The creeds are compressed summaries of the earliest eyewitness testimony; the minimal facts are a compression of the scholarly consensus.",
      "quote": "I often talk about the creeds. I have a lot I have a lot of stuff on the creeds. I often count the creeds. [S341-S343]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "R",
      "plays_role": "Phase transition — a threshold that changes state, not just degree. The conversion of a skeptic or the shift of a scholar's view (e.g., Jimmy Dunn moving right, Tony Flew's letter) is treated as a qualitative change.",
      "quote": "Read these six pages. It looks like he's converting to Christianity. [S049-S050]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "Q",
      "plays_role": "Superposition — open possibility stays unresolved until actualized. Habermas refuses to resolve the question of who is a Christian or where a person stands before God, leaving it open.",
      "quote": "I don't ever want to say whether I think so and so is a Christian or not a Christian because you're probably asking them questions about their deepest heart. [S096-S097]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "F",
      "plays_role": "Non-local correlation — related systems are no longer independent. The resurrection appearances create a correlation between Jesus and the disciples, and between the early church and later believers.",
      "quote": "I believe that the disciples saw Jesus and that he saw them and next Easter will find me in church. [S201]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "C",
      "plays_role": "Integration — the local integrator inside the product. Habermas himself is the integrator, the scholar who gathers and weighs the spectrum of views into a single cumulative case.",
      "quote": "I wrote the book. If you want to write it, you go write one. But I can tell you what I'm what I'm doing. [S307-S309]",
      "fit": "direct"
    }
